# The jev lane is an ALLOWLIST repo.
#
# The root holds ~20 vendored clones of other people's repositories, and the set grows every
# session. An opt-out list would go stale the moment a sibling pane clones the next one, and a
# nested git repo added to this tree becomes a gitlink that nobody configured as a submodule.
# So: ignore everything at the root, then un-ignore exactly what we author.
#
# Adding a new clone requires NO change here. Adding a new first-party directory does.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/AGENTS.md
!/EVAL.md
!/NEGATIVE_EVIDENCE.md
!/GATES.md
!/TESTS.md
!/.fh-agents.toml
!/githooks/
!/scripts/
!/probes/
!/foundation/
!/compaction/
!/notes/
!/.beads/
!/docs-mirror/
!/upstream/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs-mirror/ and upstream/: PROVENANCE is committed, BYTES are not.
#
# `scripts/sync-docs.sh` re-fetches the mirror and `--check` proves byte identity against the
# committed sha256 manifest. So the manifests are the reviewable artifact; the 5 MB of TypeSafe
# documentation and the nested first-party clones are reproducible, third-party, and would churn
# every diff. A fresh clone runs one command to materialize them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs-mirror/*
!docs-mirror/MANIFEST.tsv
upstream/*
!upstream/MANIFEST.tsv
!upstream/ORG-INVENTORY.tsv

# Harness and tool state that belongs to a machine, never to the repo.
.ntm/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Language caches and build output, wherever they appear under a first-party path.
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
.test-dist/
